From 3ce3d6e8b530190d5ea1e7520ff8a946e58e1b94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:17:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 33/44] hydra: do not write a parameter that carries no value

Houdini's material builders declare a shader input without authoring an opinion
on it - `float inputs:specular` with no value at all, which is what the exported
USD of a freshly built material is full of. Such a parameter can reach the
translation holding an empty VtValue, and converting one lands a zero on the
Cycles socket, overriding the default the node would otherwise keep. A specular
that was never set became a specular of zero.

Not verified by render: husk reports no available license with Houdini closed,
so this rests on reading the exported USD and the conversion path rather than on
a measurement. The change can only ever prevent a write that had nothing to
write.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hydra/material.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hydra/material.cpp b/src/hydra/material.cpp
index 22ab45ac..7474c6ff 100644
--- a/src/hydra/material.cpp
+++ b/src/hydra/material.cpp
@@ -1459,6 +1459,15 @@ void HdCyclesMaterial::UpdateParameters(NodeDesc &nodeDesc,
     }
     VtValue value = valueDs->GetValue(0.0f);
 
+    /* Houdini's material builders declare a shader input without authoring an
+     * opinion on it - `float inputs:specular` with no value at all - and such a
+     * parameter can reach here holding nothing. Converting that would land a
+     * zero on the socket and override the default Cycles would otherwise keep,
+     * so a specular of none becomes a specular of zero. Leave it alone. */
+    if (value.IsEmpty()) {
+      continue;
+    }
+
     /* See if the parameter name is in USDPreviewSurface terms, and needs to be converted .*/
     const UsdToCyclesMapping *inputMapping = nodeDesc.mapping;
     std::string inputName = inputMapping ?
